insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('IEM COLOGNE MAJOR 26','esport','Major returned to the Cathedral of Counter-Strike. The stories this tournament created will stay with fans for a very long time. NiKo finally lifted his first Major trophy with Falcons. Magixx delivered an unbelievable 1v4 clutch. m0NESY''s performance reminded everyone why he''s one of the best players in the world... and I could go on. The content from this event generated over 1 million organic impressions on my Instagram, where you can also find all of the photos and videos I shared throughout the tournament.','/assets/video/491946_ed08a9e242134ce6be6327cce400fe43.mp4','/assets/img/poster/491946_ed08a9e242134ce6be6327cce400fe43.jpg','portrait',0,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('Clash of the Stars 16','sport','Clash of the Stars 16 and Vašek''s title fight. I''m incredibly happy about the collaboration we''ve built together. I filmed Vašek''s entire journey throughout the tournament, and I had the first edit finished the very next day after the event. That video has already surpassed 97,000 views. Vašek won his fight and earned the championship belt—it looks absolutely incredible. Congratulations, my friend.','/assets/video/491946_38cbb1a761ff434393be653ede613d8b.mp4','/assets/img/poster/491946_38cbb1a761ff434393be653ede613d8b.jpg','portrait',1,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('IEM KRAKÓW 26','esport','The year 2026 marked another chapter for IEM. After many long years in Katowice, this legendary tournament is moving to Kraków. As I write this—I''ve still got goosebumps. A new chapter is here, and I''m incredibly grateful that I was able to be part of it. Thank you very much for the accreditation, and you can already check out the first video.','/assets/video/491946_59ca5df2ca994335963810a4df30b39d.mp4','/assets/img/poster/491946_59ca5df2ca994335963810a4df30b39d.jpg','portrait',2,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('IEM KATOWICE - Hall of Heroes','esport','In 2025, I went to IEM Katowice to capture the atmosphere of one of the biggest esports events in the world. Crowds cheering, lights flashing, pure focus and emotion in every match. An incredible experience full of energy, passion, and unforgettable moments.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-dhOdup2cMo',null,'landscape',3,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('STARLADDER MAJOR 2025 Budapest','esport','At the end of 2025, I still managed to attend one more event. Huge thanks to the Starladder organization for the accreditation. An atmosphere that gave me goosebumps. A spectacular run by FaZe and so many other moments I’ll remember for the rest of my life. Video coming soon.','','/assets/img/491946_0140edccc5f2419cad6cf620468af4b8.jpg','landscape',4,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('CLASH OF THE STARS Baba Jaga Promo','sport','After an agreement with Vašek (Baba Yaga), we decided that I would make a video for him from the Clash of the Stars 14 tournament. Take a look at a highlight video from the evening, where Vašek won his fight. Thank you, Vašek, for the opportunity — it was great, and I’m looking forward to further collaboration.','/assets/video/491946_5af9a881fb9242159f4ec99cbac0daea.mp4','/assets/img/poster/491946_5af9a881fb9242159f4ec99cbac0daea.jpg','portrait',5,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('RAMSON BARBER promo spot','promo','This week I spent some time at our barbershop, capturing the vibe that makes it special. The sound of clippers, smell of fresh coffee, laughter, and good energy all around. More than a haircut — it’s a place where style, confidence, and stories come together.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nJ0PC8LIzBY',null,'landscape',6,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('Speed, power and pure passion','sport','This weekend I captured the intensity on ice — blades slicing through every corner, energy rising with each play. The crowd, the speed, the emotion… everything came together in one unforgettable match.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ny3ixBGOGvc',null,'landscape',7,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('Born to Rule the Game','promo','Filming a promo spot with FK Teplice and Platinum Natural was pure teamwork and creativity. Players giving it their all, passion meeting precision — a perfect connection between sport and lifestyle.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=faNMqMeDQJU',null,'landscape',8,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('Where Every Paw Matters','promo','A weekend full of joy, wagging tails, and countless stories. Shooting at the biggest pet fair in the Czech Republic, we captured the energy, care, and love that connect people with their four-legged friends.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w1fNC0BB5nE',null,'landscape',9,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('HC Teplice Huskies','sport','Every stride on the ice told a story of effort, focus, and heart. I spent the day with the team, capturing moments where ambition meets unity — and every frame felt like pure magic.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U87QbqV7utk',null,'landscape',10,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('Awaken Your Inner Hero','promo','Creating a promo spot for Chladné Zbraně was like stepping into another world. Strength, courage, and craft — every detail designed to awaken something powerful inside.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EdbCakDebd8',null,'landscape',11,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('Chasing Glory on Ice','sport','Adrenaline, sweat, and heart — that’s what defines every match. I captured the spirit of competition, where strength and precision decide who remains standing when the final horn echoes.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C0gvJ_RZ91g',null,'landscape',12,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('STRONGHOLD SUPERHORSE','product','Promo video for the STRONGBOLD H800 Superhorse (1 pair) — showcasing a heavy-duty telescopic sawhorse built from high-grade steel. With adjustable legs, anti-slip feet, and an impressive 1,180 kg load capacity, it’s made for professionals who need strength, stability, and portability in one.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4fWiDfy8pbA',null,'landscape',13,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('CRAFTMAKER ROLLER X-Stand','product','This week I worked on a new product video for the CRAFTMAKER ROLLER X-Stand — a sleek, practical display solution for professionals. Clean lines, smooth motion, and precision in every shot. More than just a stand — it’s where craftsmanship meets perfect presentation.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8-vdxbzLN7U',null,'landscape',14,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('craftmaker work table T200','product','I created a promo video for the Craftmaker Work Table T200 — a folding, portable work table built for versatility and ease. Featuring a robust MDF top, a steel base with handy tool-holes, and a compact fold-flat design, it’s made to handle up to 100 kg and fits perfectly in a car trunk.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DIVrad6YN_k',null,'landscape',15,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('STRONGBOLD S1','product','A promo video I produced for the Strongbold S1 Portable Clamping Station — highlighting its strength, flexibility, and smart design for every workspace.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EyyFuxZps90',null,'landscape',16,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('craftmaker foldstation s20','product','A video project featuring the Craftmaker FoldStation S20 Adjustable Sawhorse and Worktop — showing how it seamlessly transforms from a sturdy sawhorse into a versatile worktable.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g0YFdihJJhE',null,'landscape',17,true);
insert into public.videos (title,category,description,video,poster,orientation,sort,published) values ('strongbold superhorse H800','product','Another video for the STRONGBOLD H800 Superhorse (1 pair) — featuring its next-generation telescopic design, high-grade steel construction, and impressive 1,180 kg load capacity.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hjy3RObUdpg',null,'landscape',18,true);

-- posts
insert into public.posts (slug,title,cover,excerpt,body,date,read_time,views,sort,published) values ('macbookm5max','Upgrading from M2 Pro to the New M5 Pro Max: Is It Worth It?','/assets/img/491946_0d9d73321191428fab9d9fc0368913c0.jpg','Today Apple introduced a new generation of MacBook Pro machines powered by the M5 Pro Max chip. As someone working in photo and video production, I decided to upgrade immediately. But the ob','<p>Today Apple introduced a new generation of MacBook Pro machines powered by the M5 Pro Max chip. As someone working in photo and video production, I decided to upgrade immediately. But the obvious question is:<strong>why upgrade when I was already using a MacBook with the M2 Pro chip?</strong>For many people, the M2 Pro is still a very powerful machine. In fact, it’s more than capable of handling most professional workflows even today.<strong>That raises a fair question:</strong>Is upgrading after just a few years really necessary, or is it simply falling for Apple’s marketing cycle?</p><br><p>In my case, the decision wasn’t just about owning the newest device. It was about performance, workflow efficiency, and future-proofing the tools I rely on every day.</p><br><p><strong>Coming from the M2 Pro</strong></p><p>My previous machine was a MacBook Pro with the M2 Pro chip. At the time I bought it, it was an excellent choice for creative work. It handled large photo libraries, 4K video editing, color grading, and heavy multitasking without major issues. For a long time, it felt like there was no real reason to upgrade. The machine was fast, reliable, and portable — exactly what you want from a laptop used in professional production. But over time, as projects become larger and workflows more complex, even powerful machines start to show their limits.</p><br><p><strong>Why Consider the Upgrade?</strong></p><p>Working in photo and video production means dealing with increasingly demanding workloads:</p><ul><li><p>higher-resolution cameras</p></li><li><p>larger RAW files</p></li><li><p>more complex video timelines</p></li><li><p>heavier use of effects, color grading, and AI tools</p></li></ul><br><img src="/assets/img/491946_0d9d73321191428fab9d9fc0368913c0.jpg" alt=""><br><br><p>Each of these things slowly increases the pressure on your hardware. While the M2 Pro was still capable, the idea behind upgrading to the<strong>M5 Pro Max</strong>is simple: reduce waiting time, improve rendering performance, and make the workflow smoother overall. Time matters when you work with media production. Faster exports, smoother playback, and better performance during editing can add up to<strong>hours saved every week</strong>.</p><br><p><strong>The Real Question: Is the Performance Difference Noticeable?</strong></p><p>This is probably the most important question anyone considering an upgrade will ask. Apple’s chip development over the past few years has been extremely aggressive. Each generation brings improvements not only in raw CPU and GPU power, but also in memory bandwidth, media engines, and AI acceleration.</p><p>For creators, the<strong>media engines and GPU performance</strong>are often the biggest game changers. If the M5 Pro Max delivers significantly faster video encoding, smoother timeline playback, and better handling of large RAW files, then the upgrade becomes less about luxury and more about productivity.</p><br><p><strong>Upgrade or Not?</strong></p><p>The truth is that upgrading from an M2 Pro is not something everyone needs to do. For many people, that machine will remain more than powerful enough for years. But if your work depends on speed, reliability, and handling increasingly demanding media formats, upgrading to the latest generation can be a strategic decision rather than an impulsive one. For me, the MacBook is not just a computer. It’s the<strong>core tool of my entire workflow</strong>. And when your work depends on your tools every single day, investing in performance can make a real difference.</p><br><p>I’ll definitely share my experience with you after a few months, once I’ve completed multiple projects on this new MacBook.</p><br><p>Štefan</p><br><img src="/assets/img/491946_7177308a8f8b4a2bbbbf2ccf0b46617c.jpg" alt=""><br><br>','11. 3. 2026','Minut čtení: 2',3,0,true);
insert into public.posts (slug,title,cover,excerpt,body,date,read_time,views,sort,published) values ('intel-extreme-masters-2025-counter-strike-katowice','Intel Extreme Masters 2025 Counter Strike - Katowice','/assets/img/491946_d58d5044f7e64fb9befecbb558c0fa0c.jpg','In February, I headed to Intel Extreme Masters in Katowice once again—this time for the fourth time overall.“It’s one of my all-time favorite events, mainly because the atmosphere inside the','<p>In February, I headed to Intel Extreme Masters in Katowice once again—this time for the fourth time overall.“It’s one of my all-time favorite events, mainly because the atmosphere inside the Spodek Arena is absolutely unreal. I already touched on that a bit in my article about IEM 2022.</p><br><p>So why write another article about the same event? In 2025, I changed my accreditation and attended as<em>media</em>for the first time. That alone made the whole experience feel different—it brought a new sense of motivation and excitement.</p><br><p>I packed all my filming gear, which honestly took up more space in my suitcase than my clothes. I didn’t want to underestimate anything, so I brought the best equipment I have at home. I mainly shoot on a Sony Alpha A7S III, along with several lenses, a drone, plenty of batteries, and lots of other accessories.</p><p>The moment we arrived at the event, I could feel the atmosphere that makes IEM famous all over the world. My goal was to capture and recreate that feeling—and judging by the stats, I think I managed to do just that :). As of today, the video has reached over<strong>120,000 views</strong>on social media.</p><br><p>You can see a preview of the video on the homepage, and you’ll also find the full version in my portfolio.</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/491946_d58d5044f7e64fb9befecbb558c0fa0c.jpg" alt=""><br><br><p>A big thank-you goes to ESL for another accreditation for their event. Katowice have another major advantage: you’re really close to the players, which means there’s plenty of room for great shots and photos. Throughout the entire event, I barely turned off the camera and hardly even had time to grab a coffee in the press room. That’s something I absolutely love—when there’s so much to film and you know the footage will be worth it.</p><br><p>NAVI fans managed to create an incredible atmosphere at this tournament, but unfortunately the team didn’t make it to the final. In the final, Team Vitality faced Team Spirit. Vitality showed their dominance and overall form and won convincingly, 3–0 on maps.</p><br><p>What I really love about ESL events is the accompanying program. Where other events sometimes struggle and there’s nothing to do between matches, ESL excels—you never know where to go first. Booths, autograph sessions, competitions, merchandise sales, and much more. I even bought official Counter-Strike trading cards myself and got really lucky—I definitely didn’t expect to pull a signed Coldzera card, limited to 5/20.</p><br><p>It was a beautiful weekend and the closing of one big chapter. IEM in Katowice is coming to an end and is moving to Krakow, where the first tournament will take place in February 2026—and I’ll be there. Once again, thank you to ESL for approving my accreditation, and I can’t wait for the new chapter in Krakow.</p><p>You can once again look forward to plenty of stories, including a daily report, one main big video, and lots of photos. I’ll be sharing everything on social media as well as here on the website.</p><br><p>See you next time,</p><p>Štefan</p><br><img src="/assets/img/491946_2bf3afa607b64907b8a9542d8db7dd32.jpg" alt=""><br><br>','15. 1. 2026','Minut čtení: 2',4,1,true);
insert into public.posts (slug,title,cover,excerpt,body,date,read_time,views,sort,published) values ('worlds-2024-league-of-legends-londýn-the-o2-aréna-1','WORLDS 2024 League of Legends - London The O2 arena','/assets/img/9184c5_38d6980615164e6b909316e869e9b06f.png','The finals took place in London, and fans had the chance to arrive early for the festival outside the arena. On-site, you could buy themed merchandise, try out the new ARAM mode, take photos','<p>The finals took place in London, and fans had the chance to arrive early for the festival outside the arena. On-site, you could buy themed merchandise, try out the new ARAM mode, take photos with cosplayers, or admire the championship trophy and winner’s ring up close. The whole event was incredibly energetic as soon as you stepped out of the metro, you were immediately immersed in the WORLDS atmosphere. Everywhere you looked, you could see team banners, interviews with developers, and a flawless side program.</p><p>The big day is here. The finals between T1 and Bilibili Gaming are about to begin. The gates of the O2 Arena open, and fans fill their seats. On every chair awaited a small gift inflatable clappers and an LED wristband, which played a big role throughout the event. The wristbands lit up automatically in colors synchronized with the action in the arena, creating an incredible visual effect. Even during the musical performance, it was clear how powerful an impression this technology would leave.</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_38d6980615164e6b909316e869e9b06f.png" alt=""><br><br><p>The opening ceremony was unforgettable. I’ve experienced many major events E3 in Los Angeles, Gamescom, ESL tournaments, and even the Fortnite Championship in the U.S. but this? This was something extraordinary. The first performance by Ashnikko set the entire arena on fire. Her choreography was phenomenal. Still, I was most excited for the next two performances, which were an absolute 11/10 for me.</p><p>Mars Atlas and Tiffany Aris delivered an unforgettable show with their song<em>Still Here</em>. The vocals, the choreography, the energy, pure goosebumps. And then came the highlight</p><p>Linkin Park in their new lineup. The entire arena erupted as the<em>WORLDS 2024</em>anthem began to play. Mike Shinoda then introduced both teams as they entered the arena one by one. Last to arrive was Faker, whose entrance sent chills through the entire crowd.</p><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_c2c846e2d14b474ab706decd0e68ef28.png" alt=""><br><br><p>I’ve read countless reviews of the opening ceremony, and many call it one of the best in history. I can only agree it was absolute perfection.</p><p>Once the ceremony ended, it was time for the matches themselves. Many expected T1 to easily defeat Bilibili Gaming, but reality was different. T1 lost the first map, immediately raising the tension in the arena. No one anticipated all five maps, yet that’s exactly what happened. T1 won the decisive map, and Faker with his team became the 2024 champions. Their journey to WORLDS was tough, but they proved why they are one of the greatest teams in history. Their ability to learn from their mistakes is incredible.</p><p>The entire event can be summed up in one word — unforgettable. If you want to experience at least a glimpse of this atmosphere, I highly recommend watching the opening ceremony recording on the League of Legends YouTube channel. You’ll see just how epic this experience was.</p><p>See you next time…</p><p>Štefan</p>','7. 11. 2025','Minut čtení: 2',20,2,true);
insert into public.posts (slug,title,cover,excerpt,body,date,read_time,views,sort,published) values ('gamescom-největší-herní-veletrh-v-evropě-kolín-nad-rýnem','Gamescom - The Biggest Gaming Fair in Europe, Cologne','/assets/img/9184c5_69ab0b318e004768a407eac7466bfe20.png','In today’s article, we’ll talk about the biggest gaming fair in Europe. Gamescom is held annually in Cologne, Germany, and is extremely popular among gamers. Unlike E3, this event is more fo','<p>In today’s article, we’ll talk about the biggest gaming fair in Europe. Gamescom is held annually in Cologne, Germany, and is extremely popular among gamers. Unlike E3, this event is more focused on the gaming community. Even though the last edition of E3 was also open to the public, it just didn’t have the same magic as this traditional event. Perhaps that’s one of the reasons why we’ll no longer see another E3 in Los Angeles.</p><p>I’ve attended Gamescom six times already, and each time it has been an incredible experience. Every year, this event offers a unique opportunity for anyone who loves games and virtual worlds to experience something special. Gamers from all around the world gather here, and the atmosphere is simply perfect. I still remember my very first year my friends and I drove there by car, not knowing what to expect. The line outside, which I remember vividly to this day, was enormous. Compared to later years, when I had media or retail access and didn’t have to wait in line, that first year was a true test of patience.</p><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_69ab0b318e004768a407eac7466bfe20.png" alt=""><br><p>If you’ve never been to this event but are considering attending this year’s edition, you’re probably wondering what to expect. You can look forward to massive halls open to everyone. There’s also a business area accessible only with accreditation, but even for regular visitors, there are countless opportunities. You can try out upcoming games, take photos with cosplayers, buy merchandise from your favorite game studios, and chat with gamers from all over the world.</p><p>One of the downsides is that if you want to try a highly anticipated game, you might end up waiting in line for several hours. The reward for your patience, however, often includes small gifts like t-shirts, stickers, keychains, or figurines. Each studio has its own marketing strategy, and some are incredibly generous with their giveaways. I remember one studio handing out graphics cards by literally throwing them into the crowd. Pretty intense like a real-life round of Hunger Games!</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_fd5494269d3b4badb45454a6c214082c.png" alt=""><br><br><p>With accreditation, you can skip the lines by scheduling appointments in advance. For example, after visiting the Genshin Impact booth, I received a press kit and had the opportunity to chat with one of the developers. There were also official cosplayers from the game on site, and their costumes were absolutely breathtaking. Each costume represents countless hours of work and dedication hats off to everyone who puts their heart into this craft.</p><br><p>Gamescom isn’t just about trying out upcoming games. There’s also a massive hall filled with merchandise. One of my favorite stops every year is the Blizzard booth. As a long-time fan of Blizzard games, especially World of Warcraft, I always make sure to bring something home as a souvenir.</p><p>Every time I leave Gamescom, I realize how incredible the gaming community truly is. Gaming and esports have skyrocketed in recent years, and today the gaming industry stands among the most profitable sectors in the world, continuing to grow every year.</p><p>You might even run into your favorite streamer or YouTuber which is another amazing part of this event. Gamescom is an experience you’ll remember for the rest of your life.</p><br><p>See you next time,</p><p>Štefan</p><br>','6. 11. 2025','Minut čtení: 2',6,3,true);
insert into public.posts (slug,title,cover,excerpt,body,date,read_time,views,sort,published) values ('e3-expo-2018-los-angeles-usa','E3 Expo 2018 Los Angeles USA','/assets/img/9184c5_e02fc7879e5d49bb807712a9a0cc54d5.png','It’s the year 2018, and I find out that this year I’ll be going to the biggest gaming expo — E3 in Los Angeles. For people who follow the gaming world, it was the most traditional and above ','<p>It’s the year 2018, and I find out that this year I’ll be going to the biggest gaming expo — E3 in Los Angeles. For people who follow the gaming world, it was the most traditional and above all the biggest event in the gaming industry. Every year, I watched from home to see what new announcements were made and what was being prepared for the future. Being there in person was a huge dream of mine. That dream was about to come true — I was heading to the USA for the first time as a marketer for a gaming retail company. The flight was long, and with my height… well, it wasn’t exactly comfortable, but I couldn’t wait.</p><p>We landed at Los Angeles Airport, went through security, and there it was — we were in America! At first, I couldn’t believe it. We arrived a few days early, so we had plenty of time to explore lots of beautiful places.</p><p>We went to Hollywood to see the famous Walk of Fame and walked around the downtown area, where the EA Play event was being held, if I remember correctly. We couldn’t miss it and there, I took a photo with Ben Irving, who was the lead producer of the game<em>Anthem</em>. Expectations for the game were sky-high, and their booth reflected that. Unfortunately, the game didn’t turn out well, but still incredible memories! We got to try many upcoming EA games and enjoyed yet another unforgettable experience.</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_e02fc7879e5d49bb807712a9a0cc54d5.png" alt=""><br><br><p>After that, we went to an LA Dodgers baseball game and later visited an LA Galaxy match  where Zlatan Ibrahimović was playing at the time. I didn’t hesitate and bought a jersey as a souvenir. Before the match, we listened to the American national anthem, followed by a fireworks show. Yet another unforgettable experience.</p><br><p>Next came trips to places like Malibu Beach, Santa Monica, and Venice Beach spots every GTA fan definitely knows. After a few more trips, it was finally time to move on to the grand event E3.</p><p>Here we go! E3 begins! Sitting inside the Microsoft Theater and seeing the Xbox presentation live was an incredible experience. I’ve been a PlayStation fan since I was a kid, but I had to admit  this was absolutely spectacular! Trailer after trailer, and the energy in the entire hall was unreal. After that, we moved straight to the main convention center, picked up our badges, and we were ready to go! The atmosphere there was absolutely perfect.</p><p>E3 was open only to journalists, influencers, and people actively working in the gaming industry. The event was not open to the general public.</p><br><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_73a32631c769453fb5dc6f060cfdc974.png" alt=""><br><br><p>Looking back, I realize I actually experienced the last year PlayStation was present at this event. We’ll talk about E3 2019 later, but by then, PlayStation was no longer there. Their presentation that year was incredible showcasing upcoming titles like<em>The Last of Us Part II</em>,<em>Ghost of Tsushima</em>,<em>Death Stranding</em>, and more. A perfect ending to a great era at this expo. We visited countless booths and tried out so many games. It’s also worth mentioning Nintendo’s booth, which was celebrating huge success with its Nintendo Switch console.</p><p>It was a wonderful week full of unforgettable experiences, and I believe the selected photos will capture that feeling too. I’m truly thankful for this opportunity, which allowed me to fulfill my childhood dream.</p><p>Until next time…</p><p>Štefan</p>','5. 11. 2025','Minut čtení: 3',6,4,true);
insert into public.posts (slug,title,cover,excerpt,body,date,read_time,views,sort,published) values ('intel-extreme-masters-2022-katowice','Intel Extreme Masters 2022 Katowice','/assets/img/9184c5_cd66dc7de23844fcb8f5a11da27a80d5.png','Another amazing event that definitely deserves its own article! I’ve had the chance to attend this tournament several times, and I even remember when League of Legends used to be played here','<p>Another amazing event that definitely deserves its own article! I’ve had the chance to attend this tournament several times, and I even remember when<em>League of Legends</em>used to be played here. Unfortunately, those days are gone, and in the following years, the organizers focused mainly on<em>Counter-Strike</em>and<em>StarCraft II</em>. I always look forward to this tournament so much, because the atmosphere in the Spodek Arena is absolutely perfect I truly wish everyone could experience it. I believe it’s exactly this atmosphere that makes the tournament appealing even to visitors who don’t normally follow gaming that closely. Personally, I was really excited because I knew G2 would be playing, and I was hoping they’d win the whole tournament. Did they even make it to the finals? You’ll find out in this new article.</p><p>The car trip to Poland is long, but manageable. You know what’s waiting for you, so you’re excited and counting down the kilometers until you finally arrive. Once again, I had the honor of receiving a GUEST pass for this event, so I didn’t have to wait in any lines    THANK YOU FOR THAT! :D Because seeing that crowd of fans, willing to stand outside in any kind of weather just to get in, is truly admirable.</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_cd66dc7de23844fcb8f5a11da27a80d5.png" alt=""><br><br><p>I check into the hotel, pick up my badge, and off I go to the first matches! This tournament featured teams like NAVI, G2, FAZE Clan, Heroic, Gambit, and many others. From the very first second, you can feel the incredible atmosphere as fans cheer their teams forward. I have to admit  I always only attend the<em>Counter-Strike</em>matches. I like<em>StarCraft II</em>as a game after all, it’s from my favorite studio,Blizzard but watching it competitively just isn’t really my thing.</p><p>The tournament spans several days, so there’s plenty of time to explore the city, and I always completely switch off my mind while I’m here. You’re “far enough away” from all work responsibilities, and I really try not to work at all just enjoy what I’ve loved since childhood. Games are a huge escape for me from all the daily work and stress, and they truly help me recharge. Plus, thanks to gaming, I’ve met so many great friends some of whom I’ve never even met in person, yet I trust them more than people I see regularly.</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_d4b8478ceb6c4fb08f861bb71f432f67.png" alt=""><br><br><p>The big day has arrived the grand finale! The entire arena is filled with special effects, a stunning trophy for the winners, and fans all hoping their favorite team will take the title. My wish came true G2 made it to the finals against FAZE! It was an incredible nail-biter, but G2, including my favorite player M0NESY, lost in the finals 3–0. FAZE Clan became the champions, winning $400,000. The celebration was absolutely unbelievable. Every year I get goosebumps, and this time was no exception. A perfectly spent weekend and I felt as happy as a little kid.</p><p>After the celebrations, the fans slowly left the arena and returned to their hotels. I decided to drive home that same day, so it was quite a tough journey and if I remember correctly, I got home around three in the morning. I opened the door to my apartment, lay down in bed, and knew this was an experience I’d remember for the rest of my life.</p><p>THANK YOU, THANK YOU, THANK YOU! It was perfect!</p><br><p>Until next time…</p><p>Štefan</p>','4. 11. 2025','Minut čtení: 3',6,5,true);
insert into public.posts (slug,title,cover,excerpt,body,date,read_time,views,sort,published) values ('esl-one-2019-kolín-nad-rýnem','ESL ONE 2019 Cologne','/assets/img/9184c5_5d49e597d69746aa821245aa15f1591f.png','In 2019, I got an amazing opportunity to attend this huge Counter-Strike event as a guest. I owe this opportunity to Martin Polášek, and I want to send a big thank you to him in retrospect! ','<p>In 2019, I got an amazing opportunity to attend this huge Counter-Strike event as a guest. I owe this opportunity to Martin Polášek, and I want to send a big thank you to him in retrospect! During this tournament, I got to experience a backstage tour where I saw how everything comes together.</p><br><p>Where exactly did I get to take a peek? I saw a lot of production rooms — to the point where you start wondering why there’s so much equipment! An event of this scale requires countless people, and it was really nice to see how much everyone loves what they do. People who aren’t involved in gaming might just think “it’s only games,” and they often don’t understand events like this.</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_5d49e597d69746aa821245aa15f1591f.png" alt=""><br><br><p>Gaming and esports have reached a global level, where professional players in some cases earn more than athletes, actors, and others. Another important aspect is the community and the atmosphere at these events. There are moments when I literally get goosebumps all over my body.</p><p>The entire event took place in the same city where the well-known Gamescom is held. We’ll definitely talk more about that event in the future as well. ESL ONE specifically took place at the Lanxess Arena — and it was absolutely packed! Fans were cheering their favorites on to victory. I couldn’t wait for it to start.</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_9054ebf06fb74ad89ec1ebf8ab4edba7.png" alt=""><br><br><p>Seeing the best CS teams in the world compete for a total prize pool of $300,000 was an incredible experience. Personally, I’m a fan of the organization Fnatic, but I also really liked Team Liquid, who ended up winning the entire tournament and taking home a beautiful $125,000.</p><p>It was another experience I’ll remember for the rest of my life. Another badge for my collection — one I’m truly proud of. Once again, thank you, Martin, for the amazing opportunity to experience all of this.</p><p>I’m also adding some photos to this article. They were taken on a phone, so I apologize in advance for the quality — I had to download them and couldn’t find the originals.</p><br><p>Until next time…</p><p>Štefan</p>','1. 11. 2025','Minut čtení: 2',12,6,true);
insert into public.posts (slug,title,cover,excerpt,body,date,read_time,views,sort,published) values ('apple-studio-display-recenze-produktu','Apple Studio Display Product Review','/assets/img/9184c5_fd0d29f126e94473b3d5dd647e4127d1.png','Today, I’m writing a slightly different type of article than usual. I want to start sharing more about my work trips on my website what I’ve experienced, the projects I’ve worked on, and the','<p>Today, I’m writing a slightly different type of article than usual. I want to start sharing more about my work trips on my website what I’ve experienced, the projects I’ve worked on, and the places I’ve created them in. But I also really enjoy sharing reviews of products I actively use. For the first one, I chose a product I bought about half a year ago.</p><p>It’s the<strong>Apple Studio Display</strong>, which I had been eyeing for quite some time. I’ve been a fan and user of Apple products since I was around 15, when I got my first iPhone 3GS. I currently work on a<strong>16-inch MacBook Pro 2023</strong>, and one of the things I absolutely love about this technology is the display. The Retina screen is a feast for the eyes. Recently, I had been connecting my work MacBook to a Dell monitor, and the “unrealistic” colors really bothered me overall, it felt like a huge downgrade.</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_fd0d29f126e94473b3d5dd647e4127d1.png" alt=""><br><br><p>I didn’t own a high-end monitor before, and I believe things would have been much better with my new MSI monitor, which I recently bought. However, I had been eyeing the<strong>Studio Display</strong>for a long time, though I hesitated because the price is quite steep for “just a display.” Apple offers two versions the first starts at around<strong>42,000 CZK</strong>, while the second, the<strong>XDR variant</strong>, is priced around<strong>133,000 CZK</strong>… yes, that much money for a monitor!</p><br><p>I went for the cheaper version, which still offers plenty of features I knew I’d appreciate. Another requirement for me was a<strong>VESA mount</strong>, so I could adjust the display position freely when needed. The advantage here is that the display can also be rotated vertically, depending on how you position the monitor similar to how it works on an iPad.</p><p>So, I purchased the Studio Display with the VESA mount version and started using it actively. The<strong>VESA mount</strong>itself must be bought separately, as it’s not included in the box. Now, after six months of use, I can share my opinion on this product.</p><p>One thing I really like and one of the main reasons I decided to buy it is that the<strong>Delta E value is below 1!</strong></p><p>What does Delta E mean? Simply put, it measures how closely the displayed color matches the color perceived by the human eye. This means you won’t have the issue of working on graphic projects where colors look one way on your screen, but after export, they appear different to your client. The<strong>quality and accuracy of delivered work</strong>are essential for me, and that’s why I see this as one of the biggest advantages.</p><p>The<strong>brightness range</strong>reaches up to<strong>600 nits</strong>, making it perfectly visible in all lighting conditions. Apple mainly designed this product for home, office, or studio use. You can easily adjust the brightness as needed it even reacts automatically depending on whether it’s day or night. The<strong>True Tone</strong>feature is, of course, included.</p><p>When I plan a videocall, I don’t need to open my MacBook the Studio Display has a<strong>12 MP ultra-wide camera</strong>with<strong>Center Stage</strong>. To be honest, I have to say that for a display in this price range, the camera quality could be better, but for regular video calls, it’s perfectly fine for me. Another great feature is that the built-in<strong>microphones</strong>isolate your voice while suppressing background noise.</p><p>The monitor also comes with<strong>six built-in speakers</strong>that support<strong>spatial audio</strong>, so any movie or music sounds absolutely fantastic.</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_f8201159d22d4d7db1ae1d63933fefa3.png" alt=""><br><br><p>The display is<strong>27 inches</strong>, has<strong>14.7 million pixels</strong>, and offers<strong>5K resolution</strong>. As I mentioned earlier, I have absolutely nothing to criticize about the display itself it’s one of the main reasons I wanted to switch to it. The colors are simply incredible.</p><p>The Studio Display is equipped with its own<strong>A3 chip</strong>, which also receives regular updates. It’s possible that Apple may roll out future improvements, so I recommend checking for updates regularly. On the back of the monitor, you’ll find<strong>three USB-C ports</strong>and<strong>one Thunderbolt port</strong>, through which you can also charge your MacBook. However, note that this may not apply to all MacBook models I recommend checking compatibility before purchasing.</p><p>The Studio Display is mainly designed for<strong>Apple devices</strong>, but it can be connected to a<strong>Windows PC</strong>as well. I actually looked into some tutorials on how to connect a gaming PC to the display to enjoy that resolution for gaming, too. Unfortunately, there are quite a few limitations in terms of what features won’t work but it<em>is</em>possible. I haven’t personally tried it yet, but maybe I will in the future. For now, I use this display primarily for<strong>work</strong>, and that’s how it will stay. For gaming, I use my<strong>MSI monitor</strong>, specifically the<strong>G32CQ4 E2 model</strong>.</p><h3>So, what’s the final verdict?</h3><p>In my opinion, the<strong>Studio Display is absolutely worth it</strong>if you already own Apple products and actively work with them. Do you regularly edit photos or videos? This display will make your workflow significantly more enjoyable. Personally, my eyes don’t get tired as easily when using it, since it adapts to the surrounding light conditions. For<strong>graphic design work</strong>, it’s also a fantastic choice. If you’re looking to invest in a device that will serve you for many years, you really can’t go wrong with this one.</p><p>However, if you’re considering buying it and your daily tasks mostly involve<strong>emails, office work, and the occasional vacation photo edit</strong>, I think a regular monitor will do the job just fine and save you quite a bit of money.</p><br><p>Until next time…</p><p><strong>Štefan</strong></p><br>','31. 10. 2025','Minut čtení: 4',6,7,true);
insert into public.posts (slug,title,cover,excerpt,body,date,read_time,views,sort,published) values ('hc-sparta-praha-vs-hc-dynamo-pardubice-02-arena-praha','HC Sparta Praha vs HC Dynamo Pardubice 02 arena - Praha','/assets/img/9184c5_6c682df719664bb2a0f355831b6b0204.png','We have another article today, this time about photography. Shooting sports is always a big challenge, but hockey is much faster compared to football. Choosing the right gear is very importa','<p>We have another article today, this time about photography. Shooting sports is always a big challenge, but hockey is much faster compared to football. Choosing the right gear is very important, as well as having at least some understanding of how this beautiful sport “works.” I can’t imagine going to shoot something like American football because I don’t know all the rules 100%, and I wouldn’t always know what exactly happened or what to expect in the next few seconds.</p><p>I have been watching and loving hockey for many years. I know the rules from A to Z, and I can say that my ability to anticipate the game is quite good. I regularly follow the NHL, and it’s also one of my photographic goals to get there professionally. Combining that with everything else I do is not easy, but I set a goal for myself this year to focus more on photography. At the moment, I spend a lot of time working with video and post-production, but that’s also my hobby. But more on that another time.</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_6c682df719664bb2a0f355831b6b0204.png" alt=""><br><br><p>I am extremely grateful for the opportunity to receive accreditation for the hockey game between HC Sparta Praha and HC Dynamo Pardubice. Photographing hockey is something completely different from football, as I mentioned above. Hockey is a fast-paced sport where every second determines whether the photos will be perfect. Overall, photographing sports matches is a big challenge for me whether it’s football, hockey, or any other sport.</p><p>I picked up my accreditation, where I also received drinks and food. That’s what I call service! Huge thanks to HC Sparta Praha for this opportunity. Sparta plays its home games in the O2 Arena, which in itself is an incredible experience. I had the chance to shoot directly from behind the plexiglass, the perfect spot for capturing great moments. We prepare the gear, set up everything needed, and here we go! The game begins…</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_7a01f371a49641dc9099ecec1baa5c51.png" alt=""><br><br><p>From the very first second, I felt completely in my element. Hockey is a beautiful sport, and I was hoping to capture some great moments. Throughout the entire game, there were plenty of goals, and it even went to a shootout. I couldn’t wait any longer I took the card out and plugged it into my MacBook. I launched Lightroom and started the import.</p><p>I knew I had captured a lot of moments worth keeping goals, fights, battles, celebrations. It turned out really well. I believe you’ll enjoy the photos too, and I’m uploading some of them to the gallery below. Unfortunately, I can’t include them all here since there were just so many.</p><br><p>It was an incredible experience, and I want to once again thank HC Sparta Praha for the amazing opportunity. I already have plenty of new articles in mind, so you can definitely look forward to what’s coming next.</p><br><p>Until next time…</p><p>Štefan</p><br>','15. 10. 2025','Minut čtení: 2',6,8,true);
insert into public.posts (slug,title,cover,excerpt,body,date,read_time,views,sort,published) values ('proč-zrovna-apple-produkty-které-mou-práci-ovlivňují-každý-den','Why Apple? Products That Influence My Work Every Day','/assets/img/9184c5_99675f4878774349b5e3b403e7da00f3.png','I’ve had this article in mind for quite some time. I’ve been using Apple products for years, and I’ll never forget what it felt like to hold my very first iPhone 3G. Since then, technology h','<p>I’ve had this article in mind for quite some time. I’ve been using Apple products for years, and I’ll never forget what it felt like to hold my very first iPhone 3G. Since then, technology has advanced tremendously, and today I do all my work exclusively on Apple devices. Why? Has Apple become a lifestyle brand? What are its biggest advantages? You’ll find out all of that in today’s article.</p><p>Today, I can’t imagine working with any other system than Apple’s. I use a 16-inch MacBook Pro with the M2 Pro chip, and it’s an absolute beast when it comes to video editing. When I tried rendering the same project on a gaming PC with Windows, the difference was striking. While the 4K render on my MacBook took just a few minutes, on the PC it took nearly half an hour. Apple’s chips, which replaced Intel, are simply in a league of their own. Everything runs fast, smoothly, and most importantly reliably. My Mac handles 10-bit 4K video at 100 FPS without a problem, even when I have Photoshop, Premiere, and After Effects open at the same time. So far, I haven’t come across a single task this model couldn’t handle.<br></p><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_99675f4878774349b5e3b403e7da00f3.png" alt=""><br><p>One of Apple’s biggest advantages is its ecosystem. Once I start working on my Mac, I can seamlessly continue on my iPad Pro, which is incredibly lightweight a big plus, since a MacBook of this size can get pretty heavy to carry around. The connection between all Apple devices is truly invaluable. No matter where you start working, you can pick up right where you left off on another device without missing a beat.</p><p>At first, I wasn’t sure if getting an iPad Pro would really be worth it, but now I can’t imagine being without it. It’s perfect for emails, office work, and overall project management. The only downside, in my opinion, is that the iPad runs on iPadOS, which lacks some of the capabilities macOS offers. Still, I understand why Apple keeps these systems separate once you figure out the ideal purpose for each device, your workflow becomes much smoother.</p><p>The Apple Studio Display is another product I’ve completely fallen in love with. I actually wrote a full review about it earlier. Some might call it overpriced, but for me, it’s the best display for professional work. Why? You can find all the details in that dedicated review, where I broke everything down.</p><p>And what about the iPhone?</p><p>Right now, I’m using the iPhone 16 Pro, which I upgraded to after a year with the iPhone 15 Pro Max. At first glance, they look almost identical, but the camera improvements were enough to convince me as someone who creates video content to make the switch. We might not be seeing revolutionary upgrades every year anymore, but for me, the advancements in camera technology are reason enough to test it out. I’m especially excited to try it at the League of Legends WORLDS finals it’s going to generate a ton of great content, so stay tuned to my website and socials!</p><br><br><img src="/assets/img/9184c5_6ab2b3c8eb4945d99c32d3d964206025.png" alt=""><br><br><p>The iPhone wouldn’t be complete without the Apple Watch. I’m using the Ultra model and I absolutely love it even though I sometimes forget to charge it :D. Its ability to measure just about everything is incredible, and the Ultra’s design finally won me over compared to the standard model, which I never really liked. I even made use of its features during a trip to Switzerland, where we hiked with a breathtaking view of Mont Blanc. At an altitude of almost 3,900 meters, you can definitely feel it. I track all my sports activities with the watch, and its integration with the iPhone is another amazing bonus.</p><p>Lastly, I have to mention the AirPods Pro Max. Some people might call them “ugly,” but for me, they were an instant yes. The sound quality is top-tier, and the noise cancellation is absolutely phenomenal. When I want to work in peace, I just put them on and I’m in my own world. At the same time, I can switch modes and stay aware of what’s happening around me when needed. In that sense, I also see the AirPods Pro Max as a lifestyle accessory one I wouldn’t easily trade for any other headphones.</p><p>Whether it’s the MacBook, iPad, iPhone, or AirPods, Apple is a reliable partner for me. Thanks to the seamless integration between devices, I can work more efficiently, quickly, and comfortably. And what’s next? I can’t wait to test the Apple Vision Pro, which I’ve already had the chance to try briefly in the past.</p><p>If I were to break down each device individually, this article would have many more pages. In the future, I’ll cover each product in a separate post, explore their advantages, and take a closer look at all the details.</p><p>Follow me on my social media and website so you don’t miss any new articles.</p><br><p>See you next time,</p><p>Štefan</p>','6. 10. 2025','Minut čtení: 4',11,9,true);

